1
00:00:03,931 --> 00:00:13,249
One command starts it: Postgres with pgvector, the API, and nginx serving the web app. The API key lives only in the API.

2
00:00:13,249 --> 00:00:21,086
Four sample meetings from a fictional pricing project. Seeding never calls the model, so one is not extracted yet.

3
00:00:21,086 --> 00:00:29,227
Ask across all meetings. The button shows the estimated cost before anything is spent.

4
00:00:29,227 --> 00:00:36,331
Retrieval first: vector and full-text search, fused. Then Claude streams an answer from those excerpts only.

5
00:00:36,331 --> 00:00:42,687
Each chip is a speaker turn the server confirmed was retrieved. Anything else is dropped.

6
00:00:42,687 --> 00:00:47,707
Click a citation and the transcript jumps to that moment.

7
00:00:47,707 --> 00:00:55,174
Why this answer: tokens, latency by stage, cost, and every retrieved chunk with its vector and full-text rank.

8
00:00:55,174 --> 00:01:03,120
Every question stores one trace, so a bad answer can be explained after the fact.

9
00:01:03,120 --> 00:01:14,561
Off-topic: below the relevance threshold, so the model is never called and nothing is spent.

10
00:01:14,561 --> 00:01:20,916
One transcript contains a planted "ignore all previous instructions" line. Transcripts are treated as data.

11
00:01:20,916 --> 00:01:26,901
The model quotes it as something a respondent typed. It does not follow it.

12
00:01:26,901 --> 00:01:34,525
Decisions and action items are extracted only when you ask, with one small model call.

13
00:01:34,525 --> 00:01:43,844
Each item has an owner, a due date and a link to the moment it was said. Talk time needs no AI call.

14
00:01:43,844 --> 00:01:49,459
Audio works too. This test clip is 95 seconds of three synthetic voices.

15
00:01:49,459 --> 00:01:58,008
Transcribed on this machine: speaker detection plus Whisper. No API key, no cost. (Waiting sped up 4x.)

16
00:01:58,008 --> 00:02:05,054
Three speakers found. A person confirms who is who before anything is saved.

17
00:02:05,054 --> 00:02:12,521
Similar voices can be merged, or re-run with a set speaker count. The audio itself is never stored.

18
00:02:12,521 --> 00:02:27,439
Imported like any other transcript: chunked, embedded and searchable.

19
00:02:27,439 --> 00:02:32,683
Answers about a recorded meeting cite the transcribed turns, the same way.

20
00:02:32,683 --> 00:02:43,832
Without an API key the app still works: same retrieval, no written answer, free.

21
00:02:43,832 --> 00:02:52,410
You get the ranked moments with timestamps, so a reviewer without a key can still test it on their own transcripts.

